diff --git a/board/stm32f4/REFERENCE-BSP.md b/board/stm32f4/REFERENCE-BSP.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6206ee5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/board/stm32f4/REFERENCE-BSP.md
@@ -0,0 +1,92 @@
+# DOS / STM32F413 candidate BSP
+
+This is a complete **application** BSP, restored from the last official panda
+revision containing F4 support and adapted to the pinned modern protocol/safety
+stack. It is not a physical identification of Mr One's C3XL and is not deployable. Reference strap mismatch clears the board pointer
+and hardware identity, without enabling board-specific outputs.
+`SOURCE-MANIFEST.json` records the complete historical F4 file inventory, source
+archive digest, extra source inputs, exclusions and licenses. Neither the
+historical archive nor its restricted Atollic linker is distributed here.
+
+The build explicitly requires `SONGPLUS_DOS_REFERENCE_CANDIDATE` and rejects
+`BOOTSTUB`. No bootloader/flash implementation, SPI provider or audio provider is
+linked. Current common USB, queues, health, heartbeat, safety and harness logic
+remain the firmware implementation; restored files provide actual Cortex-M4
+startup, 102 external interrupt slots (95 implemented wrappers and seven
+reserved slots), clock, GPIO peripheral enabling,
+ADC, OTG-FS USB, fan tachometer and board-specific timer outputs. Current common
+PWM/timer drivers are used with F4 frequencies. The bxCAN port uses modern
+packet/health layouts and the pinned opendbc safety stack.
+
+The reference pin map comes from comma's historical `board/boards/dos.h`:
+
+| Function | Reference mapping |
+|---|---|
+| CAN1 | PB8/PB9 AF8; transceiver enable PC1 active low |
+| CAN2 mux | PB5/PB6 or PB12/PB13 AF9; PC13 / PB10 active low |
+| CAN3 | PA8/PA15 AF11; PA0 active low |
+| USB OTG FS | PA11/PA12 AF10 |
+| Fan | PC8/TIM3_CH3 PWM; PA1 enable; PD2 both-edge tach |
+| Harness | PC0/ADC10, PC3/ADC13; PC10/PC11 relay outputs |
+| Supply voltage | ADC12 / eleven-to-one conversion |
+| SOM / bootkick | PC2 input / PC4 active-low kick; no reset output |
+| Siren / LEDs | PC12; PC9/PC7/PC6 open-drain active-low |
+| Camera clock | TIM1 reference waveforms; PB14/PB15 complementary outputs |
+
+The product has no driver camera. The historical PB7/TIM4 IR output is not
+configured or driven. Current-monitor readout is unavailable; zero in the legacy
+field must not be interpreted as a current measurement. Sound playback/recording,
+SPI error observation, CAN FD and non-ISO FD are unavailable. Actual transceiver,
+voltage-divider, harness, fan, oscillator and camera-clock wiring remain unknown.
+
+## Temperature observation
+
+F4 has no H7 digital temperature sensor. `lltemperature.h` uses ADC1 internal
+channel18 and VREFINT channel17, with factory calibration at 30 and 110 degrees
+C and 3.3 V. Calibration addresses and formula are independently checked against
+ST's pinned `stm32f4xx_ll_adc.h` reference and DS11581 Rev7 tables81/82. VBAT path
+is disabled because it shares channel18. APB2/2 gives 24 MHz ADC; 480-cycle sample
+time is 20 microseconds, exceeding the specified 10 microsecond minimum.
+
+All ADC conversions serialize in a critical section and have a finite 10000-poll
+bound. Timeout/bad channel makes health unavailable until reset; missing factory
+values, bad VREF or out-of-range temperatures return false. The protocol layer
+must reject the whole health response on false, never clamp it to a plausible
+value. This validates calculation and failure handling in a host register model,
+not sensor accuracy or a hardware conversion deadline.
+
+## Memory contract
+
+The F413xG/H datasheet documents 256 KiB SRAM1 at `0x20000000` and 64 KiB SRAM2 at
+`0x20040000`. The candidate uses only the lower 128 KiB: up to 122872 bytes for
+static sections, a dedicated 8192-byte stack, `fault_cookie` at `0x2001fff8`, and
+the historical boot-mode word at `0x2001fffc`. MSP is eight-byte aligned at
+`0x2001fff8`; cookies are NOLOAD and outside startup's zero range. The remaining
+192 KiB is intentionally unallocated. Static/stack separation is enforced by
+linker regions and assertions. Stack budget is a reservation; measured maximum
+interrupt nesting and target high-water instrumentation remain future work.
+
+The candidate reserves flash sector0 `[0x08000000,0x08004000)` and uses a
+conservative 1 MiB silicon flash limit. A further 136 bytes are reserved for the
+current eight-byte version trailer and 128-byte RSA signature. F4 provisioning
+and serial areas remain in OTP (`0x1fff79e0` / `0x1fff79c0`), outside this app image.
+No unknown bootstub layout or signature policy is declared compatible. Source
+support for a reserved trailer does not authorize signing, deployment or writing.
+
+## Offline checks
+
+`tests/f4_bsp/test_temperature.c` executes the actual ADC/provider against fake
+registers: calibration points/interpolation, VREF correction, invalid factories,
+range rejection, timeout and invalid-health latch. `test_bsp_gpio.c` executes
+actual DOS/GPIO/PWM/timer/fan code with register-only providers: bus orientation,
+active-low transceivers, IR absence, bootkick/siren/fan outputs, 96 MHz timing,
+tach IRQ/RPM filtering, cooldown and critical-section balance. Host register
+checks cannot establish any physical pin polarity, oscillator or USB behavior.
+
+`tests/f4_bsp/run_bsp.py` compiles and executes both suites, records compiler
+versions, exact transitive source hashes and logs, then invokes the ARM linker
+on generated fixtures. Exact static-RAM and app-flash boundaries must link;
+adding four bytes must fail both the respective memory region and explicit
+stack/signature assertions. Separate compilation must reject missing candidate
+consent and BOOTSTUB with the intended diagnostics. No ARM code is executed.
+All generated artifacts remain in a fresh caller-selected output directory.
